# Normalize all text files to LF on commit and check them out as LF on every
# platform. CRLF breaks the manifest/role parsers that read `KEY="value"`
# lines field-by-field — the trailing \r defeats the quote-strip and turns
# every field into an unmatchable literal. See commit c5dc147 for the
# parser-side defensive fix; this file is the source-side fix that keeps
# the in-tree data clean regardless of who edits it on which OS.
#
# `text=auto` tells git to auto-detect binary content and exempt those
# files from the normalization (no binaries in the repo today, but the
# rule is forward-compatible).
* text=auto eol=lf
